WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.448
Treating energy as a resource means recognizing that practical capacity is limited.

2
00:00:05.448 --> 00:00:14.376
Energy affects attention, effort, judgment, emotional control, and the ability to keep acting consistently when work becomes difficult.

3
00:00:14.376 --> 00:00:26.936
A person may have hours available and still lack the usable capacity for deep troubleshooting, careful writing, patient caregiving, creative problem solving, or calm leadership under pressure.

4
00:00:26.936 --> 00:00:30.794
Energy is different from time, motivation, and discipline.

5
00:00:30.794 --> 00:00:32.232
Time is the container.

6
00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:37.831
Energy is part of what determines what can realistically happen inside that container.

7
00:00:37.831 --> 00:00:45.624
Motivation can help someone start, and discipline can support follow-through, but neither one makes capacity infinite.

8
00:00:45.624 --> 00:00:51.980
When plans ignore energy, they often turn normal limits into a false story about personal weakness.

9
00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.990
An open calendar does not automatically mean useful capacity.

10
00:00:55.990 --> 00:01:04.085
A two-hour block after a conflict-heavy meeting may not support the same work as a protected morning block after real recovery.

11
00:01:04.085 --> 00:01:12.030
Technical work, learning, leadership, caregiving, creativity, and operations all draw from different forms of capacity.

12
00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.921
Some tasks require analysis.

13
00:01:13.921 --> 00:01:15.435
Some require patience.

14
00:01:15.435 --> 00:01:17.402
Some require social presence.

15
00:01:17.402 --> 00:01:20.050
Some require sustained physical effort.

16
00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:23.304
This course uses a practical, non-clinical frame.

17
00:01:23.304 --> 00:01:28.827
It is not medical advice, treatment guidance, or a replacement for qualified support.

18
00:01:28.827 --> 00:01:33.140
The goal is to manage energy as a system rather than a character test.

19
00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:44.791
Better energy management means matching work to capacity, reducing unnecessary drains, protecting recovery, and designing routines that make sustainable execution more likely.
